# The Vercel project builds the Next.js app in frontend/ (Root Directory =
# "frontend"), but a CLI deploy uploads from the repository root so that
# push-triggered and command-line builds see the same tree. Everything below is
# irrelevant to that build and only slows the upload.

backend/
infra/
docs/
seeds/

*.pdf
*.json.example
html-test-questions.json

# Belt and braces. These are git-ignored already, so they should never reach an
# upload — but a deploy is the last place to discover that assumption was wrong.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
